The code/ directory contains the final Python methodology used in the study.

Main entry points

run_classical_loso.py
Runs the classical object-configuration-based leave-one-scene-out experiments
using Random Forest, Extra Trees, and an SGD-based linear SVM.

run_synchronized_window_ablation.py
Compares independent microphone-channel secondary-window selection with a
synchronized multichannel alternative under the same LOSO folds, T-set,
features, and Random Forest classifier.

run_deep_learning_baselines.py
Runs the raw-signal, spectrogram, and time-averaged STFT deep-learning baselines
under the shared object-configuration LOSO protocol. The implemented models are
1D-CNN, 2D-CNN, 2D-CNN-MultiStream, LSTM, BiLSTM, LSTM-STFT, and BiLSTM-STFT.

run_cross_material_analysis.py
Performs single-source cross-material transfer and leave-one-material-out
analyses using the shared dataset, preprocessing, feature, and label modules.

run_human_empty_validation.py
Performs the matched human-present versus human-empty secondary-window contrast
analysis and generates the associated numerical outputs and figures.

plotting_scripts/
Contains plot-only utilities that generate confusion matrices, leave-one-
material-out figures, and single-source transfer heatmaps from existing result
CSV files without retraining the models.

Core package modules

config.py: sampling, window, STFT, LPVG, path, cache, and seed settings.
metadata.py: anonymous subject labels, scene names, T-sets, and feature names.
parsing.py: canonical WAV filename parser.
preprocessing.py: independent and synchronized secondary-window selection,
pre-emphasis, and per-segment peak normalization.
features.py: STFT, LPVG d=0/1/2, fusion, and feature-matrix construction.
dataset.py: WAV discovery, sample assembly, and raw-segment caching.
feature_cache.py: feature-cache generation and validation.
models.py: RF, ET, and SGD-based linear SVM definitions.
protocols.py: object-configuration LOSO fold generation.
evaluation.py: fold-level model training, prediction, and metric calculation.
reporting.py: numerical result, classification-report, and confusion-matrix
writers.
visualization.py: publication-style confusion-matrix utilities.
window_ablation.py: synchronized-window ablation implementation.
deep_learning.py: PyTorch deep-learning baselines.
cross_material.py: cross-material transfer and LOMO analyses.
human_empty_validation.py: matched human-empty control analysis.
